ar white king is most forcing and leads to quick checkmate.  \n\nReason: Q: f3-g2 leaves white king only h1 and h2 (queen covers g1, g2, h3, g3). Then with my king coming to f2 or g3 next move, mate is inevitable in a few moves (e.g., Kg3, Qh2# or Qh1#). No stalemate risk here because white king still has h1 (not checked). This is the most direct route to mate.  \n\nAnswer: Q: f3-g2'}
